WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:02.123
- Gary V.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:04.820
The biggest confusion in America in 2019

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.902
is that money is happiness,
and I want people to be happy.

00:00:07.902 --> 00:00:10.439
(audience cheering)

00:00:10.439 --> 00:00:12.856
(soft music)

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.360
My friends, until our
society redefines success

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.190
in being happy not being rich,

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.100
everybody will continue
to go down the path

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.870
that we're seeing in our society

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.493
of depression, anxiety, drugs.

00:00:31.808 --> 00:00:32.810
(audience clapping)

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:34.760
If, for some way, through
a joke, or an analogy

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.860
or a conversation here today
or answer to a question,

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.694
I can get you to start the process

00:00:39.694 --> 00:00:44.300
of genuinely being able to handle judgment

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:47.439
because you finally are exhausted.

00:00:47.439 --> 00:00:49.970
Exhausted of living your life

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:51.630
based on other people's opinions.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:54.320
You don't do things because
somebody says you're ugly

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.050
or you're stupid in a comment

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.440
and you have no idea who they are

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.360
and they're hiding between an avatar

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.690
and some bullshit name over here

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:05.103
all the way to your mom.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:10.380
That.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:11.880
That's what I spend all my time on.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.421
From this person to that person.

00:01:14.421 --> 00:01:16.440
Why is that dictating you?

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.820
They think they're doing the right thing

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.410
'cause they fucking
actually love their parents.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.243
I get it.

00:01:20.243 --> 00:01:22.963
I love my parents so
uncomfortably much it scares me.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.441
But they live it because they're appeasing

00:01:25.441 --> 00:01:29.070
lawyer, two kids, living in
this area, doing this job,

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.720
don't take risks 'cause
we told you not to.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.450
We came from a generation that
didn't so you're doing that.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.330
Or I was once an entrepreneur
and fucked it up,

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:38.030
and so we were scared,
so now you don't do that.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.408
They live for their parents.

00:01:39.408 --> 00:01:41.580
They think it's good
'cause everything's good

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.060
'cause you're doing
what your parents want.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.063
You feel like it's good.

00:01:44.063 --> 00:01:46.650
Then what starts happening is they start

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:50.150
to resent their parents
because now they're popping

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.290
to their 50th birthday,
their 60th birthday,

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.600
their 65th birthday.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.649
They get a health scare and they're like,

00:01:55.649 --> 00:02:00.110
"Fuck, I'm not doing
what I wanna be doing."

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:01.493
The question is why?

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.130
Like, I'm just trying to get to why.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:06.770
Like, who?

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:08.250
My friends, every person in here

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.810
that's not 100% happy, including myself,

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:14.710
is not doing something because
of judgment of somebody else.

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:17.980
You have to be honest with yourself

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:19.910
'cause if you're incapable of that,

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:22.610
you have no prayer of happiness.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:24.700
And being honest with yourself is hard.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.300
It's not fun to say you suck.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.870
Vulnerability is strength.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:33.297
If you took a step back and actually said,

00:02:33.297 --> 00:02:35.730
"What do I fucking like?"

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.686
I'm trying to get people to win.

00:02:37.686 --> 00:02:40.580
I'm watching real deep sadness

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:42.513
and it's not because of social media.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:45.940
Social media is not making you sad.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.779
Your insecurity's making you sad.

00:02:47.779 --> 00:02:50.311
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:02:50.311 --> 00:02:51.144
- [Man] I love you, Gary!

00:02:51.144 --> 00:02:51.977
- I love you back.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.510
My friends, this is a fucking game.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:57.640
You wanna fucking win in life?

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.670
Fall in love with losing

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.550
because most people here are scared of it.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:04.960
The number one unlock to
happiness in this room

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.250
is to go out there after this talk

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.890
and get naked about your vulnerabilities,

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:13.940
what you suck at, take
a step back, go humble.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:17.077
This is about losing and
humility at the forefront,

00:03:17.077 --> 00:03:19.130
and nobody's talking about it.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.280
There's no system.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.340
You wanna build something?

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.839
It's hard work and talent.

00:03:22.839 --> 00:03:26.922
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.580
Hard work and talent.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.208
I know what's gonna happen.

00:03:32.208 --> 00:03:33.208
This is gonna post on YouTube

00:03:33.208 --> 00:03:34.210
and I'm gonna read the comments.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.210
They'll be like,

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.214
"Yo, easy for him to say 'I'm rich'

00:03:36.214 --> 00:03:37.210
"but I'll cry in my Ferrari."

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.786
Until you're crying in your Ferrari.

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:42.490
And when you have money
and you're sad as fuck,

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:45.390
real bad shit happens
'cause that shit goes

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:48.710
from Cognac and weed

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:51.033
to cocaine and guns in your fucking mouth.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:56.050
My friends, it is time, once and for all,

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:58.150
to fucking cut the bullshit.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:00.383
We need to start talking about happiness.

00:04:00.383 --> 00:04:04.466
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:08.054
By the way, I think I should
only talk in New Jersey.

00:04:08.054 --> 00:04:09.058
- [Man] I agree.

00:04:09.058 --> 00:04:10.060
- Right?

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.062
Fuck it.

00:04:11.062 --> 00:04:12.840
(audience cheering)

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:14.600
I'm not sure I wanna talk anywhere else

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:15.922
but fucking New Jersey.

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:18.940
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.860
I fucking love you guys.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.090
On some real shit.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:24.280
I fucking love you guys on some real shit!

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.493
On some real shit.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.193
Fuck.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:38.858
Please take my energy here
today 'cause it's on rare form

00:04:38.858 --> 00:04:40.968
to get happy.

00:04:40.968 --> 00:04:43.142
Just get happy, yo.

00:04:43.142 --> 00:04:44.144
(chuckling)

00:04:44.144 --> 00:04:44.977
Fuck.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.368
Like, fuck.

